   "source": [
    "# Human Posture Classification — Summary\n",
    "\n",
    Highlighting the business problem, dataset, models, results and quick next steps without requiring full re-training."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8ccc3045",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Project Goal\n",
    "\n",
    "Classify human posture from silhouette images into four categories: bending, lying, sitting, and standing. The project compares a custom CNN built from scratch with a MobileNetV2 transfer learning model and uses Grad-CAM for interpretability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "360580ee",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "- Source: Kaggle dataset `silhouettes-of-human-posture`\n",
    "- Total images: 4,800\n",
    "- Classes: 4 balanced posture categories\n",
    "- Input shape: 128×128 RGB silhouettes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fd0aad1e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Results\n",
    "\n",
    "- Best model: Custom CNN\n",
    "- Test accuracy: 92.78%\n",
    "- Macro F1 score: 0.9284\n",
    "- Macro AUC: 0.9938\n",
    "- Inference time: ~3.5 ms per image\n",
    "\n",
    "The project also includes Grad-CAM visualizations to validate model attention and explain predictions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7fcf5f65",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What this demonstrates\n",
    "\n",
    "- Practical application of Python, TensorFlow, and Keras\n",
    "- Strong use of data processing with NumPy and pandas\n",
    "- Clear model evaluation using accuracy, F1, ROC AUC, and confusion matrices\n",
    "- Interpretability using Grad-CAM\n",
    "- Documentation and reproducibility mindset via README, requirements, and demo script"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "920fda02",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "table_path = Path('output/model_comparison_table.csv')\n",
    "if table_path.exists():\n",
    "    display(pd.read_csv(table_path))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('The model comparison table is not available in the current environment.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c0c9488f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## How to use this repo\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Install dependencies with `pip install -r requirements.txt`.\n",
    "2. Load `human-posture-notebook.ipynb` for the full analysis.\n",
    "3. Run `src/infer.py --model output/models/mobilenetv2_final.keras --image path/to/image.jpg` for a quick demo.\n",
    "4. Review `output/figures/` for training curves, confusion matrices, and Grad-CAM heatmaps."
   ]
  }
